tudents\n$sLabel\nHome\nAcademics\nAdmissions\nProspective PhD Students\nAAA\nProspective PhD Students\nProspective PhD Students\nProspective Master's Students\nGET STARTED\n1\nRequest Info\n2\nVisit\n3\nApply\nAdmission Requirements\nApplicants must submit:\nA non-refundable application fee of $85.00 USD.\nA student copy of your transcripts in English must be submitted for each post-secondary institution (college or university) that you have attended, regardless if it was for a certificate, class, intensive program or a degree. If admitted, you will be required to have each of the institutions you have attended send an Official Transcript in English directly from the institution(s) and proof that you have successfully completed your degree(s) as indicated on your application to our Office of Admission.\nIf you have attended a college or university outside of the United States, your transcripts and diplomas (if available) will need to be evaluated via course-by-course foreign credential evaluation. Please click here for further instructions.\nThree (3) comprehensive letters of recommendation.\nA 500-word typed statement of academic and professional goals.\nCV or Resume.\nAdditional documents for international students only:\nTOEFL, IELTS, or Duolingo scores (if applicable) sent directly from the testing agency. Test scores are NOT considered as official if provided by, or received via the applicant.\nOther visa requirements will be due if accepted into the program.\nFor additional information about English proficiency and transcript evaluation click here.\nGRE is NOT required.\nApplication Deadlines\nOne entry per year \u2013 Fall semester.\nFall 2027 - Priority deadline - December 1\n(Applications received after the priority deadline will be reviewed on a space-available basis)\nInternational applicants are highly encouraged to submit their completed applications as early as possible (at least 3 months prior to priority deadline) in order to ensure ample time for t